speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, in the one minute that I have I will tell the Hon. Member that the employees of Cominco Limited in Trail are very interested in the welfare of that company and in the profits. They are well aware of the massive deficit which that company carried into last year. They are also aware of the profits it made. They base their salary and wage demands in the bargaining process on profits of the company and not the losses.
That same company with that profit is now spending $260 million Canadian on a new lead smelter. It is spending $6 million on a two-part project for germanium. It is spending $28.5 million on other projects, all of which will do two things;
generate new jobs, and clean up the environment and useless by-products which were such a hazard in the past. There are two sides to every issue. This Member is prepared to give only one side.
